AB  -  Objective: To study the effect of the improving‐muscal‐trainning on idiopathic facial palsy. Methods: 56 patients of idiopathic facial palsy were randomly divided into two groups, treatment group(28 cases) and control group(28 cases), control group were given the clinical treatment and training group were given the clinical treatment and the improving‐muscal‐trainning, the signs of idiopathic facial palsy assessed in MMT and simplified‐clinical‐scale in pre‐treatment and post‐treatment, and the electromyography of facial were detected. Results: The post‐treatment scores (measured by simplified‐clinical‐ scale) of treatment group were 14.9 higher than the scores of pre‐treatment, the scores of the control group only improved 5.5 (P < 0.05); The post‐treatment scores (measured by the MMT) of treatment group were 3 higher than the scores of pre‐treatment, the scores of the control group only improved 0.8 (P < 0.05). Conclusion: The improving‐muscal‐trainning on idiopathic facial palsy may obviously improve the effect of treatment.
